ECR (Elastic Container Registry) stores Docker container images, and ECS (Elastic Container Service) runs and manages those containers at scale, handling restarts, networking, and scaling. Together they let you package an application with all its dependencies into a container once, and run that exact same environment consistently in production, either on EC2 instances or on the serverless Fargate option.

